Title: Judge's X Word Puzzle No. 12
Author: A. N. Doran
Date: 1927-07-16
Byline: Submitted by A. N. Doran, Vancouver, B. C.
Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-07-16_93/page/n35/mode/1up
Number: 12
Solution-Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-07-23_93/page/n32/mode/1up


SKELETONS#DREAM
LAVA#OPALS#HALE
ALE#H#EMITS#RUN
IE#MAP#EDICT#MA
N#SIREN#ERROR#G
#CULPRIT#RAY#BE
DARES#CREEP#CUR
RUGS#CHILD#MAGI
USE#DREAD#EAGLE
ME#IEE#LEGATEE#
S#FILMS#RISES#T
TI#STAID#NED#PA
IRE#ATLAS#L#EEL
CORN#ELMAN#ORAL
KNEES#SECONDARY


A1. Upon what foundation is the human family built? (plural). ~ SKELETONS
A9. Upon what visionary foundation is romance built? ~ DREAM
A14. Name something which is always hot stuff. ~ LAVA
A15. Name a kind of precious stones (plural). ~ OPALS
A17. Who said, "My only regret is that I have but one life to give to my country"? ~ HALE
A18. What can be found on the other side of the St. Lawrence River? ~ ALE
A20. Name a word meaning "thrown out" which often gets into crossword puzzles. ~ EMITS
A22. What should never be seen in stockings? ~ RUN
A23. What abbreviation means "that is"? ~ IE
A24. What would you buy if you wanted to see the world? ~ MAP
A26. What is another name for a proclamation? ~ EDICT
A28. Who can rarely ever be found at home these days? ~ MA
A29. Name a bewitching person. ~ SIREN
A31. What is it always a mistake to make? ~ ERROR
A32. Who is the guilty party? ~ CULPRIT
A34. What would be a good name for a bright boy? ~ RAY
A35. What word means "to have existence"? ~ BE
A36. Name something the American aviator does. ~ DARES
A37. What do the babies do to get along? ~ CREEP
A39. By what name is a poor little pup known? ~ CUR
A40. What is always being walked over by the younger generation? ~ RUGS
A41. What is Jackie Coogan? ~ CHILD
A42. What are two holy men of the East? ~ MAGI
A43. What are cigarette lighters rarely ever good for? ~ USE
A44. What causes married men to go home early? ~ DREAD
A45. Name a famous American flyer. ~ EAGLE
A46. Give an often used and misused pronoun. ~ ME
A47. What is good for a drive? ~ IEE
A48. Who usually has a hard time getting a legacy? ~ LEGATEE
A50. What are movie actresses often seen in? ~ FILMS
A52. What does a farmer do before breakfast? ~ RISES
A54. Name a note in the musical scale. ~ TI
A56. What kind of people are never flighty? ~ STAID
A58. Give a boy's nickname. ~ NED
A59. What is another name for the old block himself? ~ PA
A60. What would make any dog mad? ~ IRE
A62. Who carries the weight of the world on his shoulders? ~ ATLAS
A64. What poor fish gets int all crossword puzzles? ~ EEL
A65. Name a famous Southern beverage. ~ CORN
A67. Name a famous violinist. ~ ELMAN
A69. At what kind of combat is the female of the species supreme? ~ ORAL
A70. What are exposed on Fifth Avenue this season? ~ KNEES
A71. What adjective describes a fellow who plays second fiddle? ~ SECONDARY

D1. What was Goliath after his bout with David? ~ SLAIN
D2. What do reformers work for? ~ KALE
D3. Who was the only girl in the world? ~ EVE
D4. In what state is Baton Rouge? (abbr.). ~ LA
D5. What preposition is used to denote motion toward a place? ~ TO
D6. What is usually open to poets? ~ OPE
D7. What would some people rather make than money? ~ NAME
D8. What is a good way to get home in a hurry? ~ SLIDE
D10. What is the briefest abbreviation for people who hog the roads? ~ RH
D11. What is corn often found on? ~ EAR
D12. What is the astringent salt used in medicine? ~ ALUM
D13. Where would be a beastly place to spend the summer? ~ MENAGERIE
D16. What is the past tense of a very moving verb? ~ STIRRED
D19. What instruments give heavenly music? ~ HARPS
D21. What is another name for a morsel, a fragment? ~ SCRAP
D24. Name something that has lots of feet (plural). ~ MILES
D25. Give a preposition meaning by, by means of. ~ PER
D27. What often gets broke when the kids play around? ~ TOY
D29. Name something swell. ~ SURGE
D30. What is a recess in a wall? ~ NICHE
D32. What has every effect—in the nature of things? ~ CAUSE
D33. What do certain criminals have to stand for? (Obsolete in some sections.) ~ TRIAL
D35. What causes a soldier to give up the bunk? ~ BUGLE
D36. What would be useful if you wanted to beat it? ~ DRUMSTICK
D38. What would a young person have to wait some time to become? ~ ELDER
D39. Many a wise bird gets caught in these. ~ CAGES
D41. In what way would many an employee like to fire the boss? ~ CREMATE
D42. The foolish birds never seem to be satisfied until they get—what? ~ MATED
D44. What is the alluvial land found in the river's mouth? ~ DELTA
D45. What remains upright—in even the wildest artist's studio? ~ EASEL
D47. Give a poetic abbreviation for "it is." ~ IIS
D49. Name a spirit that isn't usually as fine as it used to be. ~ GIN
D51. What is always at the threshold? (plural). ~ SILLS
D53. Upon what are records made? ~ TALLY
D55. What is sometimes sad? (This will prove your metal.) ~ IRON
D57. What is a lady of high degree? ~ DAME
D59. What should be left alone when it's green? ~ PEAR
D61. How should the poet write "before"? ~ ERE
D63. What is a bag for plants? ~ SAC
D64. Name something that lasts a long, long time. ~ ERA
D66. Name a point on the compass. ~ NE
D68. What little word often causes an unhappy ending? ~ NO
D69. What kind of uniform does the infantry wear? (abbr.). ~ OD


